  "description": "XIVZIM crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C84 H96 Eu4 N50 O40 2+,5(H3 O1 1+),7(Cl1 1-),38(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.745-3.922 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.55-110.93°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C84H187Cl7Eu4N50O83.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
